   "success": true,
   "error": null,
   "response_text": "All green. \n\n**The bug:** In `src/click/parser.py`, `_process_opts` did:\n\n```python\nlong_opt, explicit_value = arg.split(\"=\")[:2]\n```\n\n`str.split(\"=\")` chops the string at *every* equals sign, and `[:2]` then throws away all but the first two pieces. So `--name=a=b=c` became `(\"--name\", \"a\")` \u2014 the `b=c` tail evaporated into the void. Classic off-by-`=` mistake. \ud83d\ude43\n\n**The fix:**\n\n```python\nlong_opt, _, explicit_value = arg.partition(\"=\")\n```\n\n`partition` splits on the *first* occurrence only, so everything after that first `=` lands intact in `explicit_value`. No more value amputation.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `--name=a=b=c` now delivers `a=b=c` (was `a`).\n- Parser/options tests: 119 passed.\n- Full suite: 588 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\nNo test files touched \u2014 only `src/click/parser.py`.\n\nDONE",
